String splitting and collection filtering functions
- split — splits a String by a delimiter or Regex into a List<String>.
- splitToSequence — like split but returns a Sequence for lazy processing large inputs.
- substringBefore — returns substring before a delimiter.
- substringAfter — returns substring after a delimiter.
- chunked — breaks a String or Collection into fixed-size chunks.
- windowed — produces overlapping windows from a Collection or CharSequence.
- filter — keeps elements that satisfy a predicate.
- filterNot — keeps elements that do not satisfy a predicate.
- filterNotNull — removes nulls from a Collection<T?> producing List<T>.
- filterIndexed — filter with access to element index.
- filterIsInstance — keeps only elements of a given type.
- partition — splits a collection into Pair<List<T>, List<T>> by predicate.
- takeWhile / dropWhile — keep or drop prefix elements while predicate is true.
- distinct / distinctBy — remove duplicates or deduplicate by a selector.

Common predicate and string-check helpers like it.isNotBlank
- isBlank — returns true if String is empty or only whitespace.
- isNotBlank — opposite of isBlank.
- isEmpty — true if length == 0.
- isNullOrBlank — null-safe blank check for String?.
- isNullOrEmpty — null-safe empty check for String?.
- startsWith — checks prefix.
- endsWith — checks suffix.
- contains — checks substring presence or Regex match.
- matches — Regex full-match check.
- any — true if any elements satisfy predicate.
- all — true if all elements satisfy predicate.
- none — true if no elements satisfy predicate.
- toIntOrNull / toDoubleOrNull — try parse numeric; returns null on failure.
- firstOrNull / lastOrNull / singleOrNull — safe element retrieval returning null if not found or ambiguous.

Mapping and nullable-transform helpers related to mapNotNull
- map — transform every element to a result, may include nulls if mapper returns null.
- mapNotNull — transform and drop null results, producing List of non-null values.
- mapIndexed — transform with access to element index.
- mapIndexedNotNull — index-aware transform that drops null results.
- flatMap — transform each element to an Iterable and flatten into one list.
- flatMapIndexed — index-aware flatMap.
- mapValues — transform values in a Map without changing keys.
- associateBy / groupBy — create maps using a selector from elements after mapping.
- sequenceMap / sequence operations — apply map/mapNotNull lazily on Sequence.
